From fb9640573323600c8acc2f56a0769dc5fcda60de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Liberty <mliberty@precisioninno.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 22:03:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/13] python: address review of the wheel packaging

- Guard openroadpy's re-export of odb, utl and rmp with #ifdef BAZEL.
  CMake registers them as top-level modules, so the src.* imports broke
  `openroad -python` at startup.
- //:openroad_py depends on //python/modules, so `import odb` still works
  for downstream users of the public target.
- bazel_test.sh no longer puts every src/* directory on PYTHONPATH, which
  allowed a second copy of the extension modules to load.
- Correct the comment and ORD-0105 message: destroying the current Tech
  clears the instance even while older Techs are alive.
- openroad_test frees its Tech explicitly instead of relying on immediate
  collection; wheel_test installs the wheel with pip rather than unzipping.
- Drop a stale comment left from the removed gpl extension.

Signed-off-by: Matt Liberty <mliberty@precisioninno.com>
---
